07	>On.Map	24,12,0	12
08	Display.Conversation	Guard	Halt! The mine is closed by order of the King's Steward.\No one goes through this gate without body armour on. The hobgoblins down there would gut you. I've seen it. I didn't care for it.\Unless the Steward sent you, of course.	Where can I get armour?	10	Goodbye.	21
09	End
10	Display.Conversation	Guard	The quartermaster at the keep sells leather and iron. Or tan some cowhide and make your own on a workbench.\And wear it! In your pack it won't stop a hobgoblin's axe. You'd be surprised how many ask.	Thanks.	21
11	End
12	>On.Map	11,-3,0	15
13	Display.Conversation	Guard	Keep the peace in Puddleford, citizen.\If you're looking for work, the King's Steward pays well for hobgoblin ears. Don't ask me what he does with them.\The Steward keeps the King's keep, south of here.	Any other news?	17	Goodbye.	21
14	End
15	Display.Conversation	Guard	Halt! ...ah, you look honest enough. Honest-ish. Go on in.\The Steward holds the hall while the King is away.\The quartermaster in the courtyard sells arms.	Any other news?	17	Goodbye.	21
16	End
17	>Random	50	20
18	Display.Conversation	Guard	Three of the lads were bitten by giant spiders down the old mine. The herbalist is trying to brew something for them. One of them's still screaming. That's Dennis. Dennis screams at moths.	I'll ask her.	21
19	End
20	Display.Conversation	Guard	They say a dwarf lives right at the bottom of the mine, below the hobgoblin warren. Mad, if you ask me. Nobody does ask me. That's the trouble with this job.	Interesting.	21
